course: dictionary
lesson: 3680
title: A word for a tall pole
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A flagpole is a tall pole that a flag is raised on. Its name is two words joined together: flag and pole. When a word is made from two smaller words, the parts can give you clues to its meaning.
explain: Read the sentence around the word. «At school assembly someone pulls the flagpole rope down and the flag climbs up.» The rope, the pulling and the climbing all show that the flagpole is the thing the flag goes up.
explain: Writers can also use a flagpole to help you picture something. «A cat that trots in with its tail straight up like a flagpole» means the cat's tail is tall and straight, like a pole. The writer is comparing the tail to a flagpole so you can see it clearly.
fact: A flagpole is a tall pole on which a flag is raised.
fact: «Flagpole» is a noun, and its plural is «flagpoles».
fact: Flags are sometimes flown at half-mast, which means lowered partway down the pole, to show sadness.
fact: «Bleu, blanc, rouge» are the French flag's colours: blue, white and red.
exercise: «At school assembly someone pulls the flagpole rope down and the flag climbs up.» What is a flagpole? | A kind of tall tree | *A tall pole on which a flag is raised | A small bag for carrying a flag | A rope tied to a bell
exercise: Which word is the plural of flagpole? | flagpole's | *flagpoles | flagpoleses | flagpolia
exercise: «The French flag is bleu, blanc, rouge.» In what order are the colours of the French flag? | *blue, white, red | green, white, red | red, white, blue | blue, red, white
test: «Flags are flown at half-mast to show sadness.» What does half-mast mean? | Taken down for the winter | Tied in a knot | Raised to the very top of the pole | *Lowered partway down the pole
test: «A single wheel at the top, a pulley, simply turns your downward pull into an upward lift.» What does the pulley do? | *Turns a downward pull into an upward lift | Makes the rope longer | Stops the flag from blowing | Holds the pole upright
exam: In «a cat's tail straight up like a flagpole», what does the comparison tell you about the tail? | Tangled and short | *Tall and straight | Hidden under its body | Drooping and limp
